                <pb facs="0785" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.11/3544: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commissioner at
                        Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-15T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>72. Your 220, October 14, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department has carefully avoided any responsibility in connection with the
                    so-called Petrograd Children’s Colony and cannot entertain <pb facs="0786"
                        n="686" xml:id="pg686"/> favorably any proposition looking to their exchange
                    for Americans detained in Russia, as it believes these children should be
                    returned to their parents as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
